  - Barlow Condensed (Medium, SemiBold): Copyright 2017 The Barlow Project Authors
    (https://github.com/jpt/barlow), SIL Open Font License 1.1 (BarlowCondensed-OFL.txt).
  - Big Shoulders Stencil Display: Copyright 2019 The Big Shoulders Project Authors
    (https://github.com/xotypeco/big_shoulders), SIL Open Font License 1.1 (BigShouldersStencilDisplay-OFL.txt).
  - Special Elite: by Astigmatic, Apache License 2.0 (SpecialElite-LICENSE.txt).

MakeHuman (http://www.makehumancommunity.org): the people's figures in godot/assets/figures/ were baked by tools/mh
from MakeHuman's base mesh, targets, skeleton and system assets (skins, eyes, eyebrows, eyelashes, hair, clothes),
all released under CC0 1.0 (makehuman_system_assets_cc0.zip and the MakeHuman 1.x data). No MakeHuman file is in
this repository as it was; the baked figures, and the textures painted over the CC0 originals, are CC BY 4.0 as part
of the game's assets. The MakeHuman software itself (AGPL) is not used by or included in the game.

Synthetic voices (godot/assets/audio/voice/): no recording of any real person was used, and no real person's voice
was cloned. The four neighbours' voices, in Spanish and in English, were designed from written descriptions with
Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-VoiceDesign and every line cloned from those designs with Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-Base (Qwen team,
Alibaba Cloud; Apache License 2.0); the passenger's lines were made with Kokoro-82M (hexgrad; Apache License 2.0) in
English and Qwen3-TTS in Spanish. The takes were judged with faster-whisper (MIT) and SpeechBrain's ECAPA speaker
model (Apache License 2.0). None of these models is in this repository; their licences put no restriction on their
output. Provenance of every line: tools/voices/riachuelo/.

The four neighbours' portraits (godot/assets/operatives.webp) were made with Figma's AI image generator, painted to
match the game's style; nothing was taken from an existing image.

Everything else of the game's assets is original and made for the game: the textures and interface art come out of
the scripts in tools/ (numpy, SciPy and Pillow, BSD-style licences, are used by those scripts and are not included),
the sounds out of tools/gen_audio.py (no samples are read from anywhere), the 3D icons out of tools/icons3d/, the
level layouts out of tools/dev/*_layout.py.

The buildings, monuments and streets of the Plaza de Mayo and of La Boca are drawn after the public places as they
stood in 1958; no photograph or plan is reproduced.


4. Left out of this repository
------------------------------

This repository was carved out of a larger private project, and everything of it that Hora Cero does not use was
left out: its other levels and their data, scenes, scripts, textures, sounds, voices, portraits and history
pictures, trailers and social images; its online services (a leaderboard, crash reports, a mailing list) and their
keys; its store and signing material. (Hora Cero's own launch tools, tools/trailer/horacero_* and
tools/social/horacero/, are included; what they render is not.) No file whose licence could not be established is
included.
